* Pricing a lending position\nduring an incident
** Two prices
*** Oracle price: the only one the contract reads
*** Market price: what the collateral sells for
*** Liquidatable when q × Po × LLTV < D
** Price-tracking oracles
*** Push feeds: heartbeat, deviation threshold
*** Pendle TWAP: the move must hold the window
** Constant-price oracles
*** Exchange rate: issuer loss at once
*** Published: issuer loss at the next round
*** Linear discount: never
*** Fixed: never
** Composite oracles
*** Product: any input
*** Minimum of TWAP and schedule
*** Meta-oracle: primary, then backup after a timelock
left side
** Oracle that moves
*** Liquidations at the oracle price
*** Bad debt = D − Vo / LIF
** Oracle that keeps reading
*** Nobody liquidated
*** Hidden shortfall on the lenders
*** Drain past d* = 1 − LLTV / (1 + c)
** PT collateral
*** Price (1 + y)^-T
*** Sensitivity grows with time to maturity
*** Pool sale measured from quotes
** Decision
*** Stay loses L, leaving costs C
*** Breakeven p* = C / L
*** Conditional distribution of the size
